# What NOT to upload to EAS Build — REPO ROOT edition.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS AT THE ROOT: the per-app files (apps/*/.easignore) are not
# what EAS reads. All three local builds on 2026-07-31 reported "Compressed
# project files (164 MB)" with apps/customer/.easignore present and committed —
# identical to the byte count before those files existed. In a monorepo, EAS
# archives the GIT ROOT, not the app subdirectory named by
# projectRootDirectory, so the ignore file has to live here to have any effect.
#
# DELIBERATELY COMPLETE, not a short list of the big offenders. .easignore is
# documented to take PRECEDENCE over .gitignore rather than adding to it. If
# that reading is right, a file naming only the screenshots would start
# uploading node_modules/, ios/, android/ and .env to EAS — vastly worse than
# the problem it set out to solve, and a secret leak besides. I could not
# confirm the precedence from this environment (eas-cli runs via npx and is not
# on disk), and I am not willing to bet a credential on the favourable reading,
# so this restates every rule that matters from .gitignore. Correct whether
# .easignore replaces or supplements.
#
# If you add an ignore rule to .gitignore that matters for builds, add it here
# too. A rule in only one of the two is the failure mode this comment exists to
# prevent.

# ---- Dependencies and VCS -------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/

# ---- Generated / local build output ---------------------------------------
.expo/
**/.expo/
.export/
**/.export/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
out/
landing/out/
.next/
**/.next/
apps/*/ios/
apps/*/android/
**/expo-env.d.ts
*.log
*.orig.*

# ---- Secrets. Never upload these. -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/credentials/
*.p8
*service-account*.json

# ---- Local binaries -------------------------------------------------------
*.ipa
*.aab
*.apk

# ---- Store listing material: humans need it, no build reads it ------------
# This is the ~78 MB that was being compressed and discarded on every build.
apps/customer/store-screenshots/
apps/customer/store-screenshots-clean/
apps/customer/store-assets/
apps/driver/store-screenshots/
apps/restaurant/store-screenshots/

# ---- The marketing site, which EAS never builds ---------------------------
landing/

# ---- Repo docs and tooling not needed to compile an app -------------------
docs/
supabase/
.github/
*.md

.DS_Store
